#- § §d ╔═--═ஓ๑🔮๑ஓ═--═╗§r
         §5Eternity!§r§r
 §d╚═--═ஓ๑🔮๑ஓ═--═╝§r
§8Sweetpea sat on the edge of her creaky desk chair, her fingers tracing circles on the smooth table in front of her. A flickering candle and the occasional pulse of energy from a magic crystal was the only light in her
#- §8small Tavern Office. Casting long shadows that danced off the walls. It was the middle of the night, she couldn't sleep, 
but she liked this. Deathcap always feels more alive at night and she often took this time to absorb the islands quiet wisdom.
But now, something darker loomed at the
#- §8edge of her thoughts, whispering in her mind.

§5“Sweetpea…”

§8His voice rippled through the stillness, low and velvety. 

§5ɨȶ§8 had no name that Sweetpea knew of, but when he spoke, it was as if the island itself leaned in to listen.
#- §5“Help me become whole again! Together, we could rule eternity. Think of it, our souls intertwined forever.”

§8She felt the pull again. The promise of power. Of endless devotion. He loved her, or so he 'claimed'. And Sweetpea couldn’t deny the way her heart fluttered and
#- §8how her energy changed whenever 
he was near. 

Yet, there was a coldness beneath his words. Knowing it was the 'old version' of her he wanted. She could not shake off the feeling this was all a cruel game. A trick.

§6"What will it cost?"
#- §8she asked, her voice barely more than a breath. She knew the answer before §5ɨȶ§8 even spoke. The souls. He needed them. To feed him, to make him strong enough to transform. Souls of the innocent, the guilty, any that could nourish his dark, unfinished form.
Her stomach twisted.
#- §5“You know the cost is nothing. These souls, they are meaningless. You see them as friends, but they are dots that fade in and out as each 'reset' comes to pass.”
§8He was closer now, the shadows curling tighter around the room, as if his very presence swallowed the light.
#- §5“I love every 
version of you,” 
§8he whispered again. 

§5“I would give anything to be with you. But I cannot become my true self without you. Without your magic!”

§8Sweetpea’s fingers tightened on the table’s edge. She had always been careful, 
#- §8always avoided that which tempted other witches. Dark Magic. 

She’d seen what it did to them, how it twisted their hearts, poisoned their minds until they were nothing but shells of their 
former selves.

But this was 
different, right?
#- §5ɨȶ§8 wasn’t some malevolent force trying to trick her into ruin… or was he?

She stood abruptly, the chair scraping loudly against the floor. 

§6“This is madness! 
I don’t even know who you are!” §8she said, her voice trembling.
#- §8Silence...
Heavy and suffocating.

Then §5ɨȶ§8 laughed softly, the air wrapping around her, almost painful. 

§5“Does it matter who I am? You feel it, don’t you? That is real, Sweetpea. That is all that matters."
#- §8Yes, she felt everything. The temptation to let them have what they both wanted. A forever future. No §0Darkness§8. 
No reset. Eternity. 

She snapped out of 
it and stepped back, placing distance between them. 

§6"I need to know more"
#- §6"I cannot... will not... help you unless I know the truth."

§8There was a pause, and then the shadows shifted. §5ɨȶ§8 moved closer, a form slowly taking shape in the flickering candlelight. A tall figure, still cloaked in darkness but more solid now, more... real. 
#- §8Sweetpea’s breath caught in her throat. In the back of her mind she saw a flash of the past life they spent together.

§4✮§8An explosion.§4✯

§5“You still don’t trust me,” ɨȶ §8said, more to himself than to her. Sweetpea’s hands trembled at her side.
#- §6“I need time,” 
§8she said, her voice shaking. §6“I can’t make this decision now.”

§5ɨȶ§8 lingered just out of reach. §5“Very well,” §8he said softly. §5“But time is not infinite for you Sweetpea. And the longer you wait, the harder it will be.”
§8He receded, leaving Sweetpea alone.
#- §8She collapsed back into her chair, her mind spinning.

What was he hiding? 

And could she truly resist the temptation to find out?

§7-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-§r
§5You are writing stories about me 
and you now?
#- §6I've decided to take a more... 'short story' approach to this magazine from now on.§r

§5Why the sudden shift?§r

§6Because I am NOT her.§r

    §5Her?§r

§6The 'old' Sweetpea...
            
             ... is dead.§r 🕱
