       §8The Letter!
{by QueenOfTartarus}§r
 §6╚═--═ஓ๑👑๑ஓ═--═╝§r
§cDearest Hecate, 
today I’ve happened upon one of your daughters. She is good and wise, yet I fear for her. She’s shrouded in §0darkness§r, §ca creature, I do not yet know what ails her for it is more than§r§r
#- §cthe creature, but I shall investigate. 

Ever since the 1600s, there aren’t many of your kin left, so I must treasure this rare sighting. You must guide her to safety, be once more a guiding torch much like how you guide Persephone to and fro. Guide Sweetpea,§r
#- §cto the right and safe place; where she is meant to be.

Dearest Hecate,
The creature looming over her is called§r §5ɨȶ§r; §cthus far, it hasn’t brought her any harm... but I have my reservations. 
But it seems as 
though they have symbiotic parasitic...§r
#- §cself-preservation-
based protection from one another. 

For now, I shan’t ruin their union lest it accidentally harm 
the witch.  

And this ‘§5ɨȶ§r’ creature §cis quite good fun. 

I want him. 
A new pet.§§
#- §cHecate, 
I’ve now watched on for a while; it seems your young witch suffers from occasional bouts of memory loss. I sense remnants of the old magics. A dangerous game this young witch plays. Still, perhaps it’s time for the mortals to experience
a bit of havoc.§r
#- 
     §c§oWhat good fun.§r§r


§5Ummm...§r 

§6She can have you!§r

§5You don't mean that my love. Let's not tease our audience any longer... 😏§r

§6*sigh* Okay my love 😏§r
#- §8It was a simple idea. Witch-Craft Magazine Halloween Edition. A few spooky stories but this time... written by her friends.

Eager souls 
gathering like files near a lantern. 

All she had to do was plant the suggestion, a seed in their mind.§r
#- §5ɨȶ§r §8needs souls. She can use her magic to take small amounts. They won't notice.
 
She begins to see souls more 
like... flavors.

Each one unique with 
a blend of sweetness and fear. And she 
can gather them through stories.§r
#- §8She never wanted to do this but the truth was, she didn't have much choice.

She was in love. And love makes you do strange things. 

§5ɨȶ§r is watching...

§8A book full of tales was just enough to keep §5ɨȶ§r sated.§§
#- §8Each one unwittingly giving up a tiny part of themselves.§r 

§oIt's just a bit of fun, she told them!§r

§6Is that enough yet?§r §8she said to the dark shadow in the corner. There was no answer. Only the faintest twitch, a face forming, a glimpse of eyes.§r
#- §8She felt her own energy drain. 

A piece of her in exchange for her role in this ritual.§r

§5More.§r 

§5The reader too!§r

§8The reader expected 
a thrill and a chill, 
but not this.§r
#- §8The shadow left once more. Leaving her alone again. Her heart pounding... again.

There was no 
turning back now.

When this book is made, she will enchant the pages. A subtle spell. One she wove softly, carefully. Almost reluctantly.§r
#- §8She sighed, glancing across the room where the soul lantern hung. 
Swinging too slowly.

She wrote the last 
few words of her magazine as the lantern flickered unnaturally.§r

§6§oAnother soul now stolen...§r§r
